 "input": "council food inspection, from the officer side. businesses are on the premises register with a risk score that decides how often we visit. visits are unannounced. on the day: look at handling and storage, the building condition, and management records (they should have a food safety management system like Safer Food Better Business, with fridge temperature logs). score each area, the scores convert to the 0-5 rating. letter sent with the rating and what to improve. rating published on the FSA website. the business can appeal within 21 days or ask for a re-score visit after fixing things.",
 "expect_status": "ok",
